he'd do anything for me do anything for  the kids  four months ago there was hope jason  kelk the man who had been hospitalized  by covid longer than anyone else in the  country  took his first few steps since being  admitted to hospital in march 2020  but it was ultimately to be a cruelly  false hope  his wife sue says that last month after  jason contracted two infections  and suffered a relapse which saw him  having to be put back onto a ventilator  he decided he'd had enough he couldn't  do the things he was doing  he got more and more depressed  more and more fed up with everything  nobody could tell him how what was going  to happen  you know whether he'd get back to where  he was and if he did how  long for and i think he just he just  couldn't take it anymore he just  didn't want to he just just gave up  really  i think he'd fought so hard for so long  and he just couldn't face doing it again  jason a 49 year old it professional at a  primary school in leeds  had underlying health conditions asthma  and type 2 diabetes  he knew his best prognosis would still  mean a tracheostomy  limited physical exertion and dialysis  but for months he fought on i really  didn't know he had it  had it in him he's always been a bit of  a wimp really as far as  you know if he got ill it was  dramatic you know he was dying  and you know when he really was and when  he really needed to he found  strength from somewhere and  unfortunately  it wasn't enough jason was admitted to  st james's intensive care unit  at about the same time that derek draper  the husband of tv presenter kate  garraway  was also hospitalized mr draper has  thankfully now been allowed home  to continue his recovery with long  covered it seems that we are seeing  an emerging population of about 10 to 20  percent of people who've had  carbon 19 who develop longer term  symptoms going  forward we have to define a set of  criteria where we can actually then  assign a diagnosis a label of long  clover to these  types of patients to the exclusion of  other things like hey fever or other  chronic fatigue syndrome  related causes and then we can then  develop a treatment program for them  after over 14 months of hoping and  caring for jason his death has been a  devastating blow for his widow and step  family  but sue says the memories of her  soulmate and of his bravery in his final  hours  will last forever fraser moored sky news
 

